 (M 'openai-responses-vertical-slice' `
  'A complete second wire path. queryModelResponses() converts internal messages to protocol-neutral IR, maps them to Responses input items, serialises tools with protocol:''responses'', posts the body with node https.request/http.request (deliberately NOT fetch, so TCP chunks arrive incrementally), retries once after a 401 via refreshAfterUnauthorized, parses SSE data: lines, and feeds createResponsesStreamAssembler, which emits neutral events rendered back into Anthropic-shaped stream_events. The event queue is bounded at 10000 entries with real backpressure (response.pause/resume), and body listeners/abort/settlement are owned by a dedicated lifecycle helper. The function doc explicitly enumerates what it does NOT do: retry/fallback, prompt caching, thinking config, context management, telemetry.' `
  @('bodyLifecycle.cleanup() must run in the generator finally block, including consumer cancellation at a yield','Queue overflow must pause the response, never drop events - dropping corrupts assembler state') `
  'fail-soft - every failure (config, network, non-2xx, stream error) is converted to an AssistantAPIErrorMessage yield; partial output is retained on interruption' `
  @((C 'MAX_EVENT_QUEUE_SIZE' '10000' 'src/services/api/adapters/responsesAdapter.ts:1029'),(C 'responses capabilities' 'supportsPromptCachingMarkers:false, supportsReasoningEncryptionReplay:true, supportsServerSideTokenCounting:false, supportsStrictToolSchemas:true' 'src/services/api/adapters/responsesAdapter.ts:284-291')) `
  @('src/services/api/adapters/responsesAdapter.ts:269-291,384-459,814-858,884-1154','src/services/api/adapters/responsesStreamLifecycle.ts:10-68','src/services/api/adapters/responsesTransport.ts:10-38','src/services/api/adapters/responsesStreamAssembler.ts:6-30') `
  @('src/services/api/adapters/responsesAdapter.ts','src/services/api/adapters/responsesStreamAssembler.ts','src/services/api/adapters/responsesTransport.ts','src/services/api/adapters/responsesStreamLifecycle.ts')),

 (M 'provider-registry-resolution-chain' `
  'A versioned providers.json store (v2) holds named providers of kind api-key (baseURL/apiKey/modelsURL) or subscription (subscriptionProvider/credentialRef) plus a single activeProviderId. applyActiveProviderToEnv() projects the active provider into ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_MODELS_URL (mirrored to OPENAI_*), DELETES the Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry switches so runtime provider management always routes through the direct-API path, and on fingerprint change clears the discovered-model cache, the valid-model cache and the apiKeyHelper/AWS/GCP credential caches. Removing the active provider restores a captured env snapshot.' `
  @('Subscription providers must not leave stale ANTHROPIC_* env values behind - they are explicitly deleted','Cache clearing is keyed on a JSON fingerprint, not performed on every call') `
  'fail-soft - an unreadable/corrupt store becomes an empty store; individually invalid provider entries are skipped with a debug log; unknown ids in switch/get/remove throw' `
  @((C 'PROVIDERS_FILE_NAME' "'providers.json'" 'src/utils/providers/providerStore.ts:39'),(C 'PROVIDER_ENV_KEYS' 'ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_MODEL, ANTHROPIC_MODELS_URL, OPENAI_BASE_URL, OPENAI_API_KEY' 'src/utils/providers/providerStore.ts:40-47')) `
  @('src/utils/providers/providerStore.ts:64-100,171-222,245-266,382-389','src/utils/model/providers.ts:6-14,24-39') `
  @('src/utils/providers/providerStore.ts','src/utils/model/providers.ts')),

 (M 'subscription-oauth-provider-runtime' `
  'A SubscriptionRegistry (duplicate id throws, unknown id throws) with one builtin adapter, chatgpt-codex. The adapter performs device-code OAuth (request user_code, poll the deviceauth token endpoint, exchange at /oauth/token with PKCE code_verifier), normalises tokens, persists a versioned credential through secure storage under namespace subscriptionAuth, extracts account identity from JWT claims, and exposes a request profile plus a model-catalog source. Token refresh is single-flight with a 60s expiry buffer; identity is re-derived from the id_token on refresh and silently retained if absent. The transport pins each endpoint to an exact https://chatgpt.com path and rewrites the Responses body (delete max_output_tokens/temperature/top_p; force store:false, stream:true; force include:[reasoning.encrypted_content]).' `
  @('The Codex endpoint must be exactly https://chatgpt.com with no port/userinfo/query/hash, and must match the expected pathname','The credential never leaves secure storage - only a credentialRef string is stored in providers.json') `
  'fail-closed - assertExactCodexUrl throws invalid_endpoint for any deviation; malformed stored credentials parse to null (treated as not connected); OAuth errors are typed SubscriptionError codes (oauth_denied/oauth_expired/oauth_cancelled/network_failed/refresh_failed/entitlement_denied/quota_exceeded)' `
  @((C 'CHATGPT_AUTH_ISSUER' "'https://auth.openai.com'" 'src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/constants.ts:6'),(C 'CHATGPT_CODEX_REFRESH_BUFFER_MS' '60000' 'src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/constants.ts:12'),(C 'STORAGE_NAMESPACE' "'subscriptionAuth'" 'src/services/subscriptions/credentialStore.ts:9'),(C 'device poll interval floor' 'max(interval,1)*1000 + 3000 ms' 'src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/deviceAuth.ts:70')) `
  @('src/services/subscriptions/registry.ts:3-24','src/services/subscriptions/contracts.ts:49-64','src/services/subscriptions/credentialStore.ts:9-58','src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/adapter.ts:30-77','src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/deviceAuth.ts:20-174','src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/tokenManager.ts:30-116','src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/identity.ts:47-69','src/services/subscriptions/chatgptCodex/transport.ts:98-151') `
  @('src/services/subscriptions','src/utils/secureStorage')),

 (M 'model-catalogue-discovery' `
  'For third-party base URLs, candidate /v1/models URLs are generated from ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL (version-segment aware, plus stripping of known Anthropic-compat suffixes such as /api/anthropic, /claudecode, /anthropic), tried in order with a 15s timeout, and the first OpenAI-shaped list wins. Subscription providers instead supply a ModelCatalogSource with its own headers, redirect policy and 401-refresh hook; its response is normalised across several catalog shapes (data/models/items/array/object-map; slug|id|model|name keys). The discovered list populates the model picker and seeds ANTHROPIC_MODEL via a preference-ordered selectDefaultModel.' `
